# Proposal package (part of P1)

> Purpose: turn the approved concept, design, and layouts into three deliverables the client can review and sign off. Templates: `.cursor/templates/` (`README.md` there).

## Rules

### 1. Deliverables (all in `docs/`)
| Deliverable | Format | Template | Output |
|-------------|--------|----------|--------|
| **Proposal presentation** | **React only** (Vite). Not HTML, not a single static file, not another framework | `deck-react/` | `docs/proposal/deck/` |
| **Proposal document** | **React route** `/proposal` in the same Vite app. US Letter 8.5 × 11 in, Print → PDF. Not a standalone HTML file | `deck-react/` (document view) · section outline in `proposal-doc/proposal.html` | `docs/proposal/deck/` · `proposal.pdf` |
| **Guide** | Markdown | `guide/GUIDE.md` | `docs/GUIDE.md` (skeleton in P1, finished in P5) |

### 2. Presentation (locked)
Profile → **Proposal deck** is `react`. There is no flavor choice.

- Build it from `deck-react/` (Vite + React).
- Do not ship `deck-native`, a standalone `.html` deck, or a non-React slide file.
- Same 12-slide story (order below). The product app may still be `native` HTML; that does not change this deck.

### 2b. Format to retain
The deck and the Letter page follow this chrome. Fill copy from the project files. Do not copy another product’s name, colors, prices, or screenshots.

| Keep | Deck | Letter page (`/proposal`) |
|------|------|---------------------------|
| App | Separate Vite + React app, not the product `app/` | Same app, route `/proposal` |
| Frame | One full-viewport slide. Kicker, title, lead. Cards, numbered steps, 2- and 3-column grids | Screen toolbar (hidden in print): **Print / Save as PDF**, link back to the deck |
| Motion | Top progress bar, padded counter `01 / 12`, fading hint, prev/next | Body scroll. Cover is its own first sheet |
| Keys | ← → Space PageUp/Down Home End · **F** fullscreen · **P** print · hash `#n` · swipe · click left/right edges | Print dialog hint: paper **Letter**, margins default or none, **Background graphics** on |
| Cover | Title slide may be dark; the rest stay on the page surface | Doc type, name, tagline, prepared for, prepared by, date, revised, version |
| Print | One slide per landscape page; chrome hidden | `@page` Letter, running header/footer, page numbers, tables do not split a row |
| Reduced motion | No slide animation | No smooth-scroll requirement |

### 3. Slide order
The deck walks the same headings as the Letter document (§4), in the same order. Do not invent a different slide story.

### 4. Document sections (locked — every proposal, same order)
Do not rename, drop, merge, or reorder these. Fill the blanks from this project. A section with nothing to say still appears, with one line that it does not apply.

Cover (doc type, name, tagline, prepared for, prepared by, date, version) · Contents · Quick reference (term / meaning).

