**13. Terms — same clause numbers every time**

| Clause | Title | What it must say |
|--------|--------|------------------|
| 13.1 | Relationship | Developer provides the services; client owns operations; each party handles its own taxes; billing statement and/or official receipt; withholding only if the law requires it |
| 13.2 | Intellectual property | After the full project fee is received, client owns the custom deliverables. Developer keeps pre-existing tools and generic components. Portfolio use unless the client opts out in writing. Third-party licenses stay with their vendors |
| 13.3 | Confidentiality | Non-public business, technical, and financial information. Survives **3 years** after termination |
| 13.4 | Payment terms | Fee and schedule point at Section 6. A billing statement per installment. Work or handover may wait until an open amount is cleared. No interest unless the law requires it. **Project-fee payments are non-refundable** |
| 13.5 | Payment & timeline dependency | Work starts when the kickoff payment is received, not when the proposal is signed. Handover follows clearance of the remaining fee |
| 13.6 | Timeline schedule conditions | Schedule starts at kickoff. It moves with late client inputs. Work may pause if an installment or a prerequisite is open |
| 13.7 | Client responsibilities | Timely materials and a primary contact. UAT feedback within **3 business days**. Client delay extends the timeline under 13.6 |
| 13.8 | Change control | Work outside Section 3 needs a written change order (timeline and cost) before it starts. Chat alone does not change scope |
| 13.9 | Warranty | Deliverables materially match Section 3 for the stated calendar days, starting at **final handover**. Defects on existing scope only — not new features, vendor outages, or client changes |
| 13.10 | Limitation of liability | The build is software, not a guarantee of business outcomes. Except for confidentiality breaches or willful misconduct, liability is capped at fees actually paid. No indirect or lost-profit damages to the extent the law allows |
| 13.11 | Termination | Either party, **14 days** written notice. Client pays for work done. **Amounts already paid are not refunded.** Completed artifacts within **7 business days** after amounts due are paid |
| 13.12 | Acceptance & handover | Criteria are Section 12. Deemed accepted if the client does not send a written rejection with specific defects within **5 business days** of delivery notice. Handover items are held until the final payment is cleared |
| 13.13 | End-user legal content | Developer implements consent screens and version tracking. The client writes and approves end-user terms and privacy text. The client is the personal-information controller |
| 13.14 | End-user contact — Developer not customer-facing | End users are not sent to the developer. The client’s primary contact reports defects |
| 13.15 | Governing law & disputes | Republic of the Philippines. **30 days** good-faith negotiation, then Philippine courts |

Print rules: `@page` Letter, running header/footer + page numbers, tables repeat headers and never split rows, headings never orphaned, cover has no header/footer.

